Partial preemption in the classical strategy (contract R5), behind the
PartialPreemption gate, off by default.

A preemption target can carry Remaining, the victim's workload.Info with each
shrunk PodSet's quota scaled down and its topology usage kept. Every site that
takes a victim out of the snapshot goes through one seam in
pkg/scheduler/preemption/policy/partial.go. The classical strategy offers a
victim with floors shrunk to them, evicts shrunk targets whole when the
candidates run out without a fit, and grows them back in steps during
fill-back. Victims whose reclaim target is pending are offered right after the
evicted ones, and evicted whole once the target is older than 5 minutes. A
partial target is issued as a reclaim-target annotation, never raised, without
a preemption expectation. Fair sharing and configurable preemption still evict
whole. Mirrors the seam of https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kueue/pull/17484.

Until 0008 and 0009 land, pkg/constants/{partial_preemption,reclaim_floors}.go,
pkg/workload/{partial_preemption,reclaim_floors}.go and the gate in
pkg/features/kube_features.go are stubs of their declarations; regenerate
this patch on top of them and drop the stubs.

